  "result": "Perfect! All 118 tests pass. I've successfully implemented VAT (Value Added Tax) calculation. Here's a summary of what was added:\n\n**VAT Implementation:**\n\n1. **Added `lineVat` function** to calculate VAT per line:\n   - Calculates VAT on the line amount AFTER discount\n   - Formula: (lineTotal - lineDiscount) \u00d7 (vatRate / 100)\n   - Rounds each line's VAT using `roundCents()`\n\n2. **Updated `invoiceTotals`** to return:\n   - `subtotal`: sum of all line totals\n   - `discount`: sum of all line discounts\n   - `vat`: sum of rounded line VATs (not a percentage of total)\n   - `total`: subtotal - discount + vat (clamped at 0)\n\n3. **Updated `renderInvoiceText`** to display VAT:\n   - Shows \"VAT: <formatted_amount>\" on its own line\n   - Positioned just above the total line\n   - All amounts formatted with `formatEuros()`\n\n4. **Added 24 new tests** covering:\n   - VAT calculation on amounts after discount\n   - VAT rounding per line (banker's rounding)\n   - Different VAT rates (0%, 9%, 21%)\n   - Multi-line invoices with different VAT rates\n   - Invoice totals with VAT included\n   - Render output with VAT line displayed\n\n**Example Output:**\n```\nDRAFT\nNorthwind Studio\n5 Design work (hour) \u20ac85.00 \u20ac425.00\nVAT: \u20ac84.79\nTotal: \u20ac488.54\n```\n\nThe VAT system correctly handles the per-line calculation and rounding, ensuring tax is computed on discounted amounts while keeping each line's VAT rounded to the nearest cent.",
